    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-12724",
      "problem": "Consider the following compound predicates:\n\n$x$ is even **and** divisible by $5.$ \n\n$x$ is even **or** less than $6$.\n\nExpress these compound predicates above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is divisible by $5$\n\n- $C(x):$ $x$ is less than $6$",
      "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land.$\" \n\nSo, the first sentence reads\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130221/assets/0c81e18633c3089e7c9f56464738a57dae490c70a0c8b46d116b1a8d75cd433f.svg)\n\nthat is, $A \\land B.$\n\nMoreover, the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor.$\" \n\nSo, the second sentence reads\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130221/assets/0a76866dfc078172503784c3d67c7d36abbfe3362a9af3e07e6055f168debbf4.svg)\n\nthat is, $A \\lor C.$",
